  "issue_title": "Add event-based reconstruction for mutable GitHub fields",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\nThis PR correctly drops mutable live-only GitHub fields from frozen benchmark context because current REST snapshots cannot prove their as-of-T values. The natural follow-up is to recover useful fields such as issue labels and milestone due dates only when they can be reconstructed from historical events or timeline data without leakage.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] Reconstruct issue and PR label membership as-of-T from GitHub event or timeline data.\n- [ ] Preserve the current safe behavior when timeline data is unavailable or incomplete.\n- [ ] Add regression tests covering label add/remove events before and after T.\n- [ ] Document which mutable fields are reconstructed and which remain intentionally omitted.\n\n**Pointers**: `benchmark/github_context.py`, `fetch_context_at`, `_collect_open_at`, `tests/test_github_context.py`, `docs/architecture.md`",
